Use the casbin.IEnforcer interface to allow different enforcers to be passed to the casbin middleware config.

So now we can do:
```go
ce, _ := casbin.NewSyncedEnforcer("auth_model.conf", "auth_policy.csv")
h := Middleware(ce)(func(c echo.Context) error {
	return c.String(http.StatusOK, "test")
})
```

This PR adds real values for Internet Explorer and Edge for the `imageSmoothingEnabled` member of the `CanvasRenderingContext2D` API, based upon manual testing.

Test Code Used: 
```html
<canvas id="canvas"></canvas>

<script>
	var canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
	var ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
	alert(ctx.msImageSmoothingEnabled);
</script>
```

The previous change added the units at the end of the format string, not necessarily attached to the value.

This corrects that bug.

